@baseUrl = https://localhost:49378
@alice = 30000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001
@bob = 30000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000002
@carrier = 30000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000009

# Order Processing Platform: demo script
# Start the API (profile "OrderPlatform.Api"), then send the requests from top to bottom.
# In Development the API creates the database, seeds nine products and runs the background worker itself.
# Demo sign-in: the X-User-Id header is the user, and the X-User-Role header with the value Carrier makes them the carrier.

### PART 1. The catalog (no sign-in needed)

### 1.1 Products on sale: first page, default page size 20
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/offers

### 1.2 Paging: page 2 with 4 per page (see totalCount, totalPages, hasNextPage)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/offers?pageNumber=2&pageSize=4

### 1.3 Page size above the maximum of 100: 400 validation problem
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/offers?pageSize=500

### 1.4 One product (Mechanical keyboard): net price, VAT and gross price
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/offers/20000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000003

### PART 2. The life of an order (FR1 to FR7)

### 2.1 Place an order and wait up to 5 seconds for the price.
### The request itself reserves the stock, then calculates the price: 201 with status Priced,
### subtotal, tax, shipping charge and total. Header Preference-Applied: wait=5.
# @name placed
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/orders
X-User-Id: {{alice}}
Prefer: wait=5
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "lines": [
    { "productId": "20000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000003", "quantity": 1 },
    { "productId": "20000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000005", "quantity": 2 }
  ],
  "shippingAddress": {
    "recipient": "Ada Lovelace",
    "street": "1 Main St",
    "city": "Athens",
    "postalCode": "10557",
    "countryCode": "GR"
  },
  "paymentToken": "tok_visa"
}

### 2.2 Get it a few seconds later. The worker has done the rest in the background:
### payment authorized (Confirmed), shipment prepared, payment captured (Paid), shipment dispatched (Shipped).
### statusHistory shows every change with its time. canCancel is still true: the order is not delivered yet.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/orders/{{placed.response.body.$.orderId}}
X-User-Id: {{alice}}

### 2.3 The customer tries to confirm the delivery herself: 403. Only the carrier may.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/orders/{{placed.response.body.$.orderId}}/delivered
X-User-Id: {{alice}}

### 2.4 The carrier confirms the delivery: 202. The pipeline was waiting for exactly this.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/orders/{{placed.response.body.$.orderId}}/delivered
X-User-Id: {{carrier}}
X-User-Role: Carrier

### 2.5 Get it again: Delivered, the full history from Pending to Delivered
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/orders/{{placed.response.body.$.orderId}}
X-User-Id: {{alice}}

### 2.6 Confirm the delivery a second time: 409 with code ordering.not_awaiting_delivery
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/orders/{{placed.response.body.$.orderId}}/delivered
X-User-Id: {{carrier}}
X-User-Role: Carrier

### 2.7 Place an order without waiting: 202 at once with status Pending and a Location header.
### A digital product, so no shipping charge.
# @name background
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/orders
X-User-Id: {{alice}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "lines": [ { "productId": "20000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000007", "quantity": 1 } ],
  "shippingAddress": { "recipient": "Ada Lovelace", "street": "1 Main St", "city": "Athens", "postalCode": "10557", "countryCode": "GR" },
  "paymentToken": "tok_visa"
}

### 2.8 Poll it: priced and moved on by the worker
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/orders/{{background.response.body.$.orderId}}
X-User-Id: {{alice}}

### PART 3. Security, paging and errors

### 3.1 My orders, newest first, paged. Summaries only (status, total, item count).
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/orders?pageNumber=1&pageSize=10
X-User-Id: {{alice}}

### 3.2 Another customer cannot see Alice's order: 404, not 403, so the order's existence is not revealed
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/orders/{{placed.response.body.$.orderId}}
X-User-Id: {{bob}}

### 3.3 Bob has no orders: an empty page
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/orders
X-User-Id: {{bob}}

### 3.4 Not signed in: 401
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/orders

### 3.5 Unknown product: 400 with code ordering.products_not_available
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/orders
X-User-Id: {{alice}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "lines": [ { "productId": "99999999-0000-0000-0000-000000000000", "quantity": 1 } ],
  "shippingAddress": { "recipient": "Ada Lovelace", "street": "1 Main St", "city": "Athens", "postalCode": "10557", "countryCode": "GR" },
  "paymentToken": "tok_visa"
}

### 3.6 The same product twice: 400 with code ordering.duplicate_product
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/orders
X-User-Id: {{alice}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "lines": [
    { "productId": "20000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000002", "quantity": 1 },
    { "productId": "20000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000002", "quantity": 3 }
  ],
  "shippingAddress": { "recipient": "Ada Lovelace", "street": "1 Main St", "city": "Athens", "postalCode": "10557", "countryCode": "GR" },
  "paymentToken": "tok_visa"
}

### 3.7 Invalid request (no lines, quantity rules, missing address): 400 validation problem listing every field
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/orders
X-User-Id: {{alice}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "lines": [],
  "paymentToken": ""
}

### 3.8 Unknown order: 404 with code ordering.order_not_found and a traceId that is also in the logs
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/orders/99999999-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
X-User-Id: {{alice}}

### Rate limiting is not in this script: the limit is 100 requests per minute per client.
### To see the 429 with Retry-After, set RateLimiting:PermitLimit to 3 in appsettings.Development.json and resend 3.1.

### PART 4. Cancel: the saga runs backward
### An order can be cancelled until it is delivered. Every step done so far is undone in reverse order.

### 4.1 Place an order and wait for the price. A second later the worker has shipped it.
# @name toCancel
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/orders
X-User-Id: {{alice}}
Prefer: wait=5
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "lines": [ { "productId": "20000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001", "quantity": 1 } ],
  "shippingAddress": { "recipient": "Ada Lovelace", "street": "1 Main St", "city": "Athens", "postalCode": "10557", "countryCode": "GR" },
  "paymentToken": "tok_visa"
}

### 4.2 Cancel the shipped order: 200 with status Cancelled. The parcel is recalled, the payment is refunded,
### the shipment is cancelled and the stock is released. statusHistory ends with Shipped, then Cancelled.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/orders/{{toCancel.response.body.$.orderId}}/cancel
X-User-Id: {{alice}}

### 4.3 Cancel it again: 409 with code ordering.cannot_cancel
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/orders/{{toCancel.response.body.$.orderId}}/cancel
X-User-Id: {{alice}}

### 4.4 Bob cannot cancel Alice's order: 404
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/orders/{{toCancel.response.body.$.orderId}}/cancel
X-User-Id: {{bob}}

### 4.5 A delivered order is final: cancel the order of Part 2: 409 with code ordering.cannot_cancel
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/orders/{{placed.response.body.$.orderId}}/cancel
X-User-Id: {{alice}}

### 4.6 Place an order on hold: it stops before the payment, stock reserved, nothing charged. 201, Priced.
# @name held
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/orders
X-User-Id: {{alice}}
Prefer: wait=5
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "lines": [ { "productId": "20000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000002", "quantity": 2 } ],
  "shippingAddress": { "recipient": "Ada Lovelace", "street": "1 Main St", "city": "Athens", "postalCode": "10557", "countryCode": "GR" },
  "paymentToken": "tok_visa",
  "holdBeforePayment": true
}

### 4.7 Release it: 202. The payment is authorized next and the order continues.
### (Or cancel it here instead: only the stock is released, because nothing else was done yet.)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/orders/{{held.response.body.$.orderId}}/release
X-User-Id: {{alice}}

### 4.8 Get it a few seconds later: Shipped
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/orders/{{held.response.body.$.orderId}}
X-User-Id: {{alice}}

### 4.9 Release it again: 409 with code ordering.not_on_hold
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/orders/{{held.response.body.$.orderId}}/release
X-User-Id: {{alice}}

### PART 5 (optional). A rejected order
### Add "MONITOR-27" to FakeExternalSystems:Inventory:OutOfStockSkus in appsettings.Development.json and restart.

### 5.1 Out of stock: 201 with status Rejected and no price. Nothing was reserved or charged.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/orders
X-User-Id: {{alice}}
Prefer: wait=5
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "lines": [ { "productId": "20000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000004", "quantity": 1 } ],
  "shippingAddress": { "recipient": "Ada Lovelace", "street": "1 Main St", "city": "Athens", "postalCode": "10557", "countryCode": "GR" },
  "paymentToken": "tok_visa"
}
